# Allure results.
#
# A symptom, not a design: the build files say these go to
# `<module>/build/allure-results/` and set `allure.results.directory` to say so,
# but the Allure 2.x JUnit listener resolves its own directory relative to the
# forked JVM's working directory and ignores that key (it is allure-kotlin's
# spelling). The result lands in `<module>/allure-results/` — outside `build/`,
# so the entries above did not cover it, and ~10k files sat untracked in
# `git status` after a local run.
#
# Ignoring the symptom is not the fix; see `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, which
# uploads `*/build/allure-results/**/*` — the path that is never written to —
# with `if-no-files-found: ignore`. Filed as an issue rather than fixed here.
**/allure-results/

# KSP generated
**/ksp/

# Local Kiwi TCMS stand (infra/kiwi)
# TLS-ключ и самоподписанный сертификат — per-machine runtime state, как и
# volumes Postgres: коммитить их нельзя (секрет в репозитории), а генерируются
# они одной командой ./infra/kiwi/gen-tls.sh, которую вызывает up.sh.
infra/kiwi/tls/
infra/kiwi/secrets.env

